From: Felicitas Pojtinger <felicitas@pojtinger.com>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 22:31:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GIR: Default to MIT, rename docs tag to `puregotkdocs`, and relicense the examples to LGPL-3 to be able to include docs
---
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 03da4a5deb683e73f0151ce4cb1ac1820e7432c2..ecde335ef7464aab7a366ac2d047167ada22eae8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -136,8 +136,8 @@ puregotk itself is licensed under [MIT](./LICENSE).
 
 The generated bindings under [`v4`](./v4/) are available under two licenses, and the one that applies depends on how you build:
 
-- By default (`go build`), the bindings include documentation comments copied from upstream projects like GTK, which are licensed under [LGPL-3](./LICENSE.LGPL). Because of these comments, the bindings as built are covered by LGPL-3, and you must comply with its terms.
-- If you build with the `nodocs` tag (`go build -tags=nodocs`), the documentation comments are stripped at build time, leaving only puregotk's own code. The bindings as built are then covered by MIT.
+- By default (`go build`), the bindings exclude documentation comments copied from upstream projects like GTK. The bindings as built are covered by MIT.
+- If you build with the `puregotkdocs` build tag (`go build -tags=puregotkdocs`), the bindings include the documentation comments, which are licensed under [LGPL-3](./LICENSE.LGPL). Because of these comments, the bindings as built are covered by LGPL-3, and you must comply with its terms.
 
 # Acknowledgements
 * [Purego](https://github.com/ebitengine/purego) and the ebitengine team for their great work
